<ServiceTypePage
  title="Watch Appraisal | Shelton Watch | Bethlehem PA"
  description="Watch appraisal services in Bethlehem PA — fair market context, condition notes, and documentation. From $50. By appointment."
  h1="Watch Appraisal | Shelton Watch Services Bethlehem PA"
  serviceType="Watch Appraisal"
  serviceDescription="Written watch appraisal and valuation consultation for insurance, estate, or buy/sell decisions."
  answer="An appraisal should translate your watch into clear language: what it is, what condition honestly means, and what similar pieces have been doing in the market — without fairy tales. Many straightforward appraisals start around $50; complex estates or extensive documentation requests are quoted upfront."
  formSuffix="-appraisal"
  faqs={[
    {
      q: 'Do you appraise for insurance?',
      a: 'We can provide documentation suited to insurer conversations — clarify what your carrier requires when booking.',
    },
    {
      q: 'Can you appraise a non-running watch?',
      a: 'Yes — condition and authenticity notes adjust accordingly; function affects value context.',
    },
    {
      q: 'Is an appraisal the same as an offer to buy?',
      a: 'No — appraisals document context; purchase offers are separate conversations if you choose.',
    },
  ]}
>
  <h2>What’s included</h2>
  <p>
    Identification notes, condition assessment, market context in plain language, and a written summary you
    can forward to insurers, family members, or your own records — without pressure to sell.
  </p>
  <h2>When to book</h2>
  <p>
    Estate sorting, pre-sale clarity, divorce documentation, and “is this even real?” moments are all valid
    reasons — bring whatever paperwork exists, but absence of box and papers is common.
  </p>
